Mocha (Xiaomi Mi Pad 1, Tegra K1) LineageOS 21 patch set
========================================================

Every change this device tree needs outside of `device/xiaomi/mocha` lives here
as a patch, grouped by the LineageOS source project it belongs to. Nothing in
this directory is built into the image; the scripts apply the series to the
source tree after a `repo sync`.

Layout
------

  patches/<repo path>/NNNN-<slug>.patch

`<repo path>` is the project path inside the Android tree, so
`frameworks/av/*.patch` targets `$ANDROID_TOP/frameworks/av`. `NNNN` is the
apply position inside that project and `-<slug>` repeats the commit subject.
The scripts glob `*.patch`, sort by path and apply in that order, so the numeric
prefix alone decides the order within one project.

Scripts
-------

  patches/check.sh      validate the series without touching any worktree
  patches/install.sh    apply the series (check first, roll back on failure)
  patches/uninstall.sh  reverse only the patches from this series

All three locate the Android root relative to their own path, so they can be
run from anywhere. `--only <repo path>` restricts a run to one project, e.g.

  patches/check.sh --only frameworks/av
  patches/install.sh --only frameworks/native
  patches/uninstall.sh --only frameworks/av

`check.sh` uses a throwaway Git index per project, so dependent patches see the
patches before them without changing files or the real index. It prints one of:

  APPLIED   the change is already in the worktree
  READY     applies cleanly, not applied yet
  COVERED   the change is already included by an earlier patch
  CONFLICT  does not apply; the diff is printed

`install.sh` runs `check.sh` first and aborts if anything conflicts. It applies
in the same order and, if a patch fails mid-way, reverses only the patches it
applied during that run. `uninstall.sh` reverses in reverse order and never runs
`git checkout` or `git clean`, so local work is preserved.

Source tree dependencies
------------------------

Two projects come from personal forks instead of the LineageOSUL organisation,
because that organisation is read-only for this account
(`permissions.push=false`). The local manifest pins:

  frameworks/av      -> 380583067/android_frameworks_av      lineage-21.0-mocha
  frameworks/native  -> 380583067/android_frameworks_native  lineage-21.0-mocha

Those branches contain exactly the patches below for the corresponding project:

  frameworks/av      0001, 0031, 0033, 0035, 0041, 0042, 0043, 0050
  frameworks/native  0001

If the manifest is switched back to `LineageOSUL/android_frameworks_{av,native}`
at `lineage-21.0`, run `install.sh` after `repo sync` and the tree ends up in the
same state. Keeping both in sync matters: the device tree assumes the changes
are present either way.

What the patches are for
------------------------

frameworks/av
  0001  re-enable the software OMX nodes (the NVIDIA OMX store hides them)
  0031  accept YVU420 semi-planar from the camera
  0033  ACodec: resolve empty vendor parameters (upstream LineageOS fix the
        mocha tree was missing; without it getVendorParameters loops over an
        empty key list and spams OMX failures)
  0035  use 64-bit usage for native_window_set_usage
  0041  fix the OMX buffer leak on lock timeout
  0042  SoftwareRenderer: fall back when gralloc has no lockYCbCr
  0043  skip the broken NVIDIA h264 encoder
  0050  Codec2: make c2.android.* software video decode work on the legacy
        Tegra gralloc0 (this is what lets `debug.stagefright.ccodec=2` work):
        - add GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_TEXTURE only for CPU_WRITE + YUV allocations,
          so SurfaceFlinger can sample the decoder output while BLOB/CSD
          buffers stay untouched (HW_TEXTURE on those makes gralloc lock()
          return -ENOSYS and codec start() throws)
        - fall back to plain lock() when lockYCbCr() is missing, passing only
          the SW access bits
        - describe YV12 as planar Y/V/U instead of interleaved UV (the old
          description swapped red and green on screen)

system/sepolicy
  0001  two gaps in the system-private policy this board needs and vendor
        policy cannot express (both domains live in
        system/sepolicy/private, so no device-side rule can name them):
        - linkerconfig reads the NVIDIA /vendor blobs while building the
          linker namespaces
        - misctrl reads its own property block (upstream only grants set_prop)
        This is the only patch series outside the device tree that touches a
        system-private domain; everything else is done in device sepolicy.

frameworks/native
  0001  three display/binder compatibility changes bundled together:
        legacy camera HIDL/AIDL interfaces in kDownstreamManualInterfaces,
        format/size/usage logging when SurfaceFlinger blacks a layer out, and
        persist.sf.force_gpu_composition (the Tegra HWC blob crashes the
        composer during surface teardown; a userspace reboot loop follows)

The remaining directories hold the small compatibility fixes needed to build
LineageOS 21 for this device: frameworks/base, system/core, hardware/broadcom,
hardware/interfaces, lineage-sdk, packages/*, prebuilts/gcc, build/make and
vendor/lineage.

Working tree notes
------------------

The author keeps the longer explanatory comments in Chinese in the local
working copy; the commits pushed to GitHub carry the English wording. If the
tree shows those files as modified while `git diff` only touches comments, that
is expected - `git checkout -- <file>` restores the committed English version.

Removed entries and why
-----------------------

Patches whose target change is already present upstream were dropped, because
they blocked a forward application of the series while contributing nothing.
None of the files below exist in this directory any more; the names are kept
only so that an older build log can still be matched:

* frameworks/av/0032-omx-bqhelper...patch.disabled targeted bqhelper files that
  no longer exist in this LineageOS 21 checkout.
* frameworks/av/0034...patch was a 2017 Qualcomm patch for
  OMXNodeInstance::freeNode and was never applied by install.sh.
* hardware/lineage/interfaces/0001, 0003, 0004 were already fully present in
  the checked-out LineageOS 21 source; verified line by line against HEAD.
* hardware/lineage/interfaces/0002...patch.disabled was superseded by the same
  upstream changes.
* packages/modules/adb/0001-hidl-transport...patch.disabled (the earlier HIDL
  rewrite attempt) is superseded by the legacy FunctionFS implementation
  already present in the checked-out source. The currently applied adb fix is
  `0001-adb-fix-legacy-functionfs-offline-transport-detached.patch`, which is
  a different change: it stops the legacy transport from reporting the USB
  endpoint as detached while the host is still probing it.

Note on frameworks/av/0041
--------------------------

The upstream Qualcomm commit assumed the Mutex::Autolock in
OMXNodeInstance::freeNode() was acquired before the mActiveBuffers check. In
this tree the check does not exist yet, so the patch could only be applied in
reverse. It has been regenerated from the actual tree difference: it now
inserts the mActiveBuffers free before the lock is taken, which is the same
end state that was built and tested on the device.
